Z||000003||AusFiero||07-18-2001||12:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>same as over there aus, about 10 times too much   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL Roger. From the first reply I think we are paying cheaper. My late Bro-Inlaw paid $27,000 for a new Fatboy customised to the hilt about 3 years ago (Was his I am dying of cancer, so stuff it I will buy one before I do arrangement). So that was about $13,500 US new. Old Sportsers can be had for about US$3000<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||07-18-2001||03:17 PM||||If he got a new cusomized FatBoy for $13,000 US that is one helluva deal! Mine was $17,900 on the sticker in 97 before anything was done to it... Here in Nashville we have one of the better shops I have seen. We have 6, but Boswell's is the best and I have been to shops all over the country!<BR>Boswell's has been around almost as long as HD...<P>Never a waiting list at Boswell's. Can't believe that some people still wait on a list to get a Harley... and prices are usually around $5k lower than anywhere else on new bikes. New FatBoys from the factory are listing just under $20k.. About a grand more for RoadKings, which will be my next one!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||07-19-2001||07:08 AM||||Im not into motorcycles myself, I had a small one years ago for about 2 months. I decided it was too ez to get splattered. I think anything with only 2 wheels (essentially a powered bicycle) shouldnt cost over $2,000 or  $3,000 new. I may be missing something, but I cant see how it could possibly cost more than a car. All is just my opinion of course.||||reg||1
